retton Woods agreement\n# This remained fixed until 1967\n# So the official rate in 1964 was exactly 2.80 USD per GBP\n\n# Therefore:\n# USD/GBP = 1/2.80 = 0.357142857... (or we can just use the direct interpretation)\n\n# The question asks for USD/GBP, so if we interpret it as \"how many USD equals 1 GBP\"\n# then it's 2.80, or if \"how many GBP equals 1 USD\" it's 1/2.80 = 0.3571\n\n# Converting from USD to GBP:\n# If we have a amount in USD and want to convert to GBP using USD/GBP rate:\n# GBP = USD / (USD per GBP) = USD / 2.80\n\n# This is equivalent to: GBP = USD * (GBP per USD) = USD * 0.3571\n\n# Both give the same result\n\nresult = 305852.8560936027\ngbp_via_division = result / 2.80\ngbp_via_multiplication = result * (1/2.80)\n\nprint(f\"Result in GBP (via division by 2.80): {gbp_via_division}\")\nprint(f\"Result in GBP (via multiplication by 0.3571): {gbp_via_multiplication}\")\n\n# Round to nearest whole number\nprint(f\"Rounded: {round(gbp_via_division)}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
